          "rationale": "The Agreement imposes no most-favoured-nation obligation on the Company. The only pricing/fee provisions (Sections 3.1–3.4) set a fixed revenue-share (30% of Net Sales above $11,000 per month) with payment, reconciliation and audit mechanics, and contain no obligation for the Company to extend HDI its best or most favourable terms, to match a third party's offer, or to disclose terms given to others. The only \"no less favorably\" comparison in the document runs in our favour: Section 1.8 obliges HDI to \"promote the Site and Deerskin Products no less favorably than it promotes HDI's catalog titles\" — a Vendor-side obligation benefiting us, which we do not flag. The exclusivity/brand-licence provisions in Section 6 restrict the Company's use of the \"Deerskin\" brand online, but that is an exclusivity term, not an MFN or right-to-match mechanic, and belongs to the exclusivity rule rather than being flagged twice here. The preferred position (no Customer MFN benefiting Vendor) is therefore met, so no redline is proposed.",
